# Design

- One shell. Chat is the product; Status and Skills are secondary rooms.
- Compose shadcn primitives from `src/components/ui`. Do not invent a
  parallel button, card, or menu.
- Never hand-edit `src/components/ui/*`. Add or update only via
  `npx shadcn@latest add …` (use `--overwrite` when restoring stock).
- Theme changes belong in `src/index.css` CSS variables only. Feature
  code may pass layout `className` to primitives; do not fork colors,
  radius, or typography inside `ui/`.
- Custom widgets (GazeHero, ActionStream, ModelPicker) live outside
  `src/components/ui/`.
- GazeHero sits left of the operator name. Companion only; maps Hermes
  run state (`idle` / `attention` / `thinking` / `success`).
- Sidebar primary nav (`SIDEBAR_NAV`) holds Status, Skills, and future
  rooms; conversations fill the scrollable middle; footer holds quotas,
  host, gateway counts, then identity.
- Streaming turns keep `ActionStream` open so tool commands are visible
  as they start.
